rdks.mail - e-mail utilities
----------------------------

at the moment it contains two modules, some small utilities,
one BIG CLI program, and two packages that parse very specific
parts of an e-mail!!!

modules:

  * outlook:  deals with the (annoying) Thread-Index header.
  * content:  deals with MIME content transfer encodings
      including...
         - VERY flexible quoted-printable encoding!!!
         - VERY strict decoder (probably even a bit too strict)!!!
  * headers:  deals with RFC 822/2822/5322 message format
      including:
         - FULL PARSE TREE REPRESENTATION!!!
         - very minimal yet strict parser of Message IDs
  * contrib:  my reaction to https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/121515
      this includes...
         - convenient drop-in substitutes (at least i tried to :/)
         - has patches i personally see fit
         - MAY BE BUGGY. MAY BE VERY UNFORGIVING.
         - not tested enough (tho good enough for me!)

utilities:

  * parse-thread-index:  CLI for the outlook module.
      run with: `python -m rdks.mail.utils.parse_thread_index`
      or simply `parse-thread-index` or navigate to the utils/
      directory and run `./parse_thread_index.py`

  * mail-tree:  cheap thing that replicates Mutt's view-attachment output
      (i'm surprised there isn't an easy cli that does this =.=)
      depends on humanize <https://pypi.org/project/humanize/>
        (install with  pip install humanize~=4.9
                 or    pip install "<URI to this repo>[tree]" )
      optionally wcswidth <https://pypi.org/project/wcwidth/>
        (install with  pip install wcswidth
                 or    pip install wcswidth)

program!

  * compose.py:  composes RFC 5322 e-mails with MIME version 1.0
      depends on rdks-list <https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail.git>
        (install with  pip install "<URI to this repo>[compose]" )

installation is a bit harder due to compose.py depending on
rdks.list, but this should work:

    git clone https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail.git
    # depending on where your python/pip3 command lives
    # you MAY have to change pip into pip3, python -m pip, etc...
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    pip install -e ./rdks-mail

(of course you could clone rdks-list too and... but i think you
 already know how to do that)

remote version:

    pip install git+https://git.rapidcow.org/rdks-mail.git@main
